# Skill execution (installed skills)

Task is **not** complete until:

| Skill | Done when |
|-------|-----------|
| **excalidraw-diagram** | `.excalidraw` → PNG rendered, images **viewed**, layout fixed |
| **word-document** | DOCX validates; explicit table styling (docx-js) or one python-docx path; deliver **`.docx` only** (no generator beside deliverable unless user asks) |
| **powerpoint-presentation** | PPTX validates; **`thumbnail` every deck** (grid + `--per-slide` 150 DPI), images **viewed**, overflow fixed; `office-system` installed if missing |
| **spreadsheet-document** | `.xlsx` delivered; if formulas used: `office_tools.py recalc` → JSON `status: success` (zero formula errors); `office-system` for recalc |
| **pdf-document** | Deliver requested `.pdf`; form fills: run validation scripts per `references/forms.md` |

**PowerPoint is not done** when the `.pptx` exists—only after layout preview (or user waives visual QA).

- **PPT:** LibreOffice Impress + Poppler every delivery → `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office-system`
- **Word (new):** npm `docx`; LibreOffice only for PDF / `accept`
- **Excalidraw:** Playwright via `bash scripts/install_deps.sh excalidraw`

## Dependencies

| Target | Command | For |
|--------|---------|-----|
| Office Python | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office` | validate, extract, unpack/pack |
| Excalidraw | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh excalidraw` | PNG render |
| LibreOffice + Poppler | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh office-system` | **all PPT deliveries**, XLSX `recalc`, DOCX `accept`, conversions |
| PDF Python (pypdf, etc.) | `bash scripts/install_deps.sh pdf` | pdf-document scripts |
| npm `docx` / `pptxgenjs` | manual | new Word / new PPT |

## Office toolkit

```bash
cd skills/_shared/office-tools
uv run python3 office_tools.py validate deck.pptx --auto-repair
uv run python3 office_tools.py thumbnail deck.pptx /tmp/preview --cols 4
uv run python3 office_tools.py thumbnail deck.pptx /tmp/preview --per-slide /tmp/slides --dpi 150 --no-grid
```

PPT details: `skills/powerpoint-presentation/references/layout-preview.md`.
